        "delegation_parent": "R/B",
        "integration_sources": [],
        "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "Using byte-addressable adjacency rows and a legal SIMD reduction over independent comparisons within each verifier row may reduce bit-proxy overhead and accelerate permutation checks without changing permutation traversal or output.",
        "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
          "files": [
            "src/brute_isomorphism.cpp"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Changed the adjacency matrix elements from vector<bool> proxies to zero-initialized unsigned bytes.",
            "Applied an OpenMP SIMD bitwise-AND reduction to the independent inner-loop comparisons, retaining the original row-by-row early return and Heap permutation order."
          ]
        },
        "status": "valid",
        "mean_seconds": 0.007665722320477168,
        "commit": "6f419d73a460a2234d4ce35fcad1814c0c530e66"
      },
      {
        "id": "9bd09382f9094cf0",
        "role": "C",
        "parent_id": null,
        "delegation_parent": "R/C",
        "integration_sources": [],
        "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "For larger graphs, batching Heap-order permutations allows OpenMP static work sharing across independent exact verifications; degree-signature rejection can skip many adjacency checks, while serial emission preserves output order. Keeping small cases serial should avoid parallel setup overhead.",
        "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
          "files": [
            "src/brute_isomorphism.cpp"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Keep permutation generation sequential in the existing Heap order, buffer candidates in bounded batches, and verify independent candidates with an OpenMP static parallel-for.",
            "Precompute adjacency-row degree counts and reject mappings with mismatched degrees before performing the exact adjacency comparison.",
            "Emit matches serially in candidate order and retain the original sequential path for graphs with fewer than nine vertices."
          ]
        },
        "status": "valid",
        "mean_seconds": 0.009511638743182024,
        "commit": "c6072924faaa3544b5baa23cc41538573a2f5856"
      },
      {
        "id": "0ca33e5452d140cb",
        "role": "A",
        "parent_id": null,
        "delegation_parent": "R/A",
        "integration_sources": [],
        "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "Storing each adjacency matrix in one contiguous row-major buffer of 64-bit words should reduce row-allocation and pointer overhead while keeping each verifier's source-row scan compact, improving memory locality without changing the permutation search.",
        "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
          "files": [
            "src/brute_isomorphism.cpp"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Replaced vector-of-vector<bool> adjacency storage with a contiguous row-major packed-bit matrix; kept permutation generation and adjacency comparison order unchanged."
          ]
        },
        "status": "valid",
        "mean_seconds": 0.00741594098508358,
        "commit": "b238a82a71ae4ddd213c75804b4a22936b966600"
      },
      {
        "id": "45dc7e3e4ea841d3",
        "role": "B",
        "parent_id": "f8c35db1bcd447ca",
        "delegation_parent": "R/B",
        "integration_sources": [],
        "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "After preserving the identity fast path, SIMD-computed vertex degrees can cheaply reject degree-incompatible permutations, while a sorted degree-multiset check rejects impossible graph pairs before exhaustive traversal without changing Heap order or output.",
        "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
          "files": [
            "src/brute_isomorphism.cpp"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Compute each adjacency-row degree once with an independent SIMD reduction, only after the existing identity fast path fails.",
            "Compare sorted degree multisets before permutation traversal to reject graph pairs that cannot be isomorphic.",
            "Use a legal bitwise SIMD reduction over mapped vertex degrees to skip permutations that cannot be isomorphisms before the existing adjacency verifier."
          ]
        },
        "status": "valid",
        "mean_seconds": 0.007806888781487942,
        "commit": "fb722288cfbba94039a02401840de379e4741bb4"
      },
      {
        "id": "4d99b0f1c532433d",
        "role": "C",
        "parent_id": null,
        "delegation_parent": "R/C",
        "integration_sources": [],
        "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "For larger graphs, one persistent OpenMP team with dynamic chunks can reduce repeated team-startup overhead and balance permutation verifications whose early exits vary. A bounded candidate batch preserves exact Heap permutation order for output; byte-packed contiguous adjacency storage avoids vector<bool> proxy accesses. Small graphs remain serial via the OpenMP threshold.",
        "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
          "files": [
            "src/brute_isomorphism.cpp"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Replace vector<bool> rows with a contiguous byte adjacency matrix.",
            "Generate Heap permutations in bounded batches and verify candidates using one persistent OpenMP team with schedule(dynamic, 4), enabled only for n >= 24.",
            "Emit successful permutations serially in original candidate order."
          ]
        },
        "status": "valid",
        "mean_seconds": 0.013076856111486753,
        "commit": "4919e103f26432f2aecebfe0720562fa21e53e97"
      },
      {
        "id": "d219bc71afaa448f",
